# Implementation Notes - ToolkitSync

## SyncedModel Macro Interface
The macro must expand properties into observable storage, recording any modifications to a metadata storage dictionary.

```swift
@attached(member, names: arbitrary)
@attached(peer, names: overloaded)
public macro SyncedModel() = #externalMacro(module: "ToolkitMacros", type: "SyncedModelMacro")
```

Expanded structure sample:
```swift
// Expands to include:
public var dirtyFields: Set<String> = []
public var syncHash: String = ""
```

## Conflict Resolution Implementation
Interface matching the design token structures:
```swift
public struct SyncConflict {
    public let entityName: String
    public let recordId: String
    public let localRecord: [String: Any]
    public let remoteRecord: [String: Any]
}

public protocol ConflictResolver {
    func resolve(conflict: SyncConflict) -> [String: Any]
}
```

## Background Task Registration
Standard implementation logic using `BGTaskScheduler`:
```swift
import BackgroundTasks

public final class BackgroundSyncScheduler {
    public static func register(taskIdentifier: String, syncBlock: @escaping () async -> Void) {
        BGTaskScheduler.shared.register(forTaskWithIdentifier: taskIdentifier, using: nil) { task in
            guard let appRefreshTask = task as? BGAppRefreshTask else { return }
            
            let work = Task {
                await syncBlock()
                appRefreshTask.setTaskCompleted(success: true)
            }
            
            appRefreshTask.expirationHandler = {
                work.cancel()
                appRefreshTask.setTaskCompleted(success: false)
            }
        }
    }
}
```
